      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/morning_blessings/lefikhakh">
        <tei:div facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n38.jpg">
          <tei:pb ed="1965" n="8" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n38.jpg"/>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:lefikhakh"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n38.jpg" n="8"/>Therefore we are obliged to thank Thee, to praise Thee, to glorify Thee, to bless, sanctify and offer praise and thanks to Thy Name. Fortunate are we, how fair is our portion, and how delightful is our destiny and how beautiful is our inheritance. <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:lefikhakh/ashreinu"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n38.jpg" n="8"/>Fortunate are we that early and late, evening and morning, we say twice every day: <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
        </tei:div>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
